# chorus golden vector: handshake finish, protocol v2 message type 0x22.
#
# Committed, and never written by a test. Any implementation of chorus protocol v2 must
# produce these exact bytes from the canonical input in handshake_finish.fields, and recover
# exactly those fields from them (docs/protocol.md, "Version 2").
#
# Format: whitespace separated hex bytes, '#' starts a comment.
# Test-only keys (the four X25519 secrets in the .fields file) are public: never use them
# for a real device. The Noise prologue is the 7 bytes of handshake_init before the Noise
# message: 43 48 52 53 00 02 01. Noise_XX_25519_ChaChaPoly_SHA256 (noiseprotocol.org, rev 34).

# frame header: type 0x22, payload length 85 (0x0055), big-endian
22 00 55

# noise, Noise message 3 (-> s, se): the endpoint's static public key, encrypted, and its tag
98 47 1A 57 B5 1F 7C 06 F7 EA BF CD 22 FD A2 67
CE 80 FC 43 BE B4 8C 4B E5 CF 91 46 91 61 F9 96
B0 25 8A EE 48 AE E5 B9 A3 85 3D A1 2E 57 E0 88

# the payload, encrypted: the endpoint id (length byte, then "chorus-endpoint-test") and a 16-byte tag
70 96 8B 02 2D E7 C1 2B 58 A7 BD 3C B0 F0 11 46
8B 35 B3 04 29 34 34 F3 30 26 A0 DA 5B DA C4 BA
F1 72 86 8D B5
